    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0061" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d9-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-06-01">1 June 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister to President Roosevelt. Personal and top secret. Number 688. Your
                        546.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d9-f2"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>5. I am indeed sorry to hear the long time that must elapse before we meet on
                    your programme. When the immediate situation in <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Overlord</hi> clarifies I would make an
                    effort to meet you at Quebec or Bermuda. The former seems easier if this were
                    agreeable to you. It would probably be better for me not to come in to the
                    United States as you approach the election crisis or our enemies might try to
                    make mischief.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d9-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d9-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Military Attaché, London, via Army channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d9-f2" n="2" xml:id="d9-f2-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi></p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
